  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 acc, showing that (a) multiprofile with avgpool outperforms singleprofile and transformer aggregation, and (b) upgrading the RNA encoder from PCA to scVI yielded a meaningful +0.059 gain. However, we have no data on the scGPT encoder, leaving open whether a different learned representation could further improve performance. Question: config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) isolates the encoder effect under the same profile and aggregation settings that produced the best result, giving a clean three-way encoder comparison (PCA vs scVI vs scGPT) at the strongest configuration. Why this is the best next step: It tests a single variable (encoder) while holding the two most important settings (multiprofile, avgpool) fixed, directly informing whether the scVI representation is near-optimal or whether scGPT offers a further gain. This knowledge is critical before committing budget to multimodal fusion experiments, which would otherwise confound encoder choice with fusion strategy."
